Also shown is \((p+\bar{p})/h\) ratio from the Au+Au minimum-bias collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{{}_{NN}}}=130\) GeV [18]. The \((p+\bar{p})/h\) ratio from minimum-bias Au+Au collisions [18] at a similar energy is about a factor of 2 higher than that in d+Au and p+p collisions for \(p_{T}\)\({}^{>}_{\sim}\)2.0 GeV/c. This enhancement is most likely due to final-state effects in Au+Au collisions [9, 24, 19, 20, 22, 23]. The ratios show little centrality dependence in d+Au collisions, as shown in Table 4.1 and Figure 4.4. For \(p_{T}<2.0\) GeV/c, the ratio in \(\rm p+\bar{p}\) collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{{}_{NN}}}=1.8\) TeV [80] is very similar to those in d+Au and p+p collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{{}_{NN}}}=200\) GeV.

