are many models trying to explain this baryon excess in Au+Au collisions [9, 24, 19, 20, 22, 23]. In the following baryon production mechanism will be discussed.

#### \(\bar{p}/p\) ratio vs \(p_{T}\)

In 200 GeV Au+Au collisions, \(\bar{p}/p\) ratio was observed to be flat with \(p_{T}\) till intermediate \(p_{T}\) range [14], as shown in Figure 5.6. The baryon junction model [24] tried to explain it by using junction anti-junction production with jet quenching, on the basis of pQCD calculation [24] where the \(\bar{p}/p\) ratio decreases with \(p_{T}\) in p+p collisions. The curve from pQCD calculation [24] is also shown in Figure 5.6. However, \(\bar{p}/p\) ratios in d+Au and p+p collisions in our data show to be flat with \(p_{T}\) within errors. Anyway, the precise measurement with more statistics in p+p and d+Au collisions is needed to address this issue.

